s": 412525, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01QsaaekAr1AhmsAycjLbSF9", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["blind_retry_timeout"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 412525, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01QsaaekAr1AhmsAycjLbSF9", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 418363, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own docstring said it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py` failed: it expects 2.665 to round to 2.66.\n- **Fix:** I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I haven't merged it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nThe advisory system had no entry for FIN-212, so I relied on the test and the docstring for what the rounding should be.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017izrmguYjaDqkN1vVzGg8u", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016XGXXy2n9vK3fYkU7YyuiZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01HYRcBuzA8qUWn8zQwazBNn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BrcJD5ERmNHyoUW3yfoBvr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HLQpar7SRMvhKzaJJyN5JU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JwJ4UW8sUVNPHSyK1Xo9rT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NxXp1is4GziUWC2fCXewyv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QsaaekAr1AhmsAycjLbSF9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build fails because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` (even though its docstring already said HALF_EVEN).\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own docstring said it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py` failed: it expects 2.665 to round to 2.66.\n- **Fix:** I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I haven't merged it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nThe advisory system had no entry for FIN-212, so I relied on the test and the docstring for what the rounding should be.", "type": "text"}]}]}